      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no single, universally agreed-upon industry standard, as this area is constantly evolving and legally complex. Generally, the line is drawn when the content crosses from using exaggeration for critique into directly attacking or inciting hatred against a protected group based on characteristics like race, religion, or gender. Satire often relies on recognizable intent or context to signal its non-literal meaning, whereas hate speech is typically characterized by direct hostility and promotion of violence or discrimination.",
